            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> I ran Mason > Update outdated modules (by pressing U) -> mini.ai displayed the following message:\n\nPressing `U` works for me. Judging by the screenshots, you pressed `i<BS>` either in Visual mode (like after `v`) or Operator-pending (like after `y`).\n\nI am pretty sure that the 'mason.nvim' error has nothing to do with 'mini.ai'.\n\n> Due to an error with yank function, I was not able to copy the full message instead clipping the screen.\n\nThis also doesn't feel relevant to 'mini.ai' or there needs to be more information. Using non-existing textobject will show a warning (which this is). To not have its side effects affect other activity, use only existing textobjects.",
